                <pb facs="1170" n="1050" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg1050"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/880: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Representative on Special Mission in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-09T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 9,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>80. Your 75, November 8, 5 p.m.</p>
                <p>Lee, Higginson and Company sending representative Cuba Friday or Saturday if
                    assured Cuban Government wishes competitive bidding. Other bankers also
                    interested. Please telegraph as early as possible manner in which loan will be
                    negotiated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
